=   entry .Event   what a browser sees: an instance found on the link, or lost from it
-     detail
+     detail

-         `Found(instance)` is an instance appearing — its PTR record arriving in the cache —
-         and `Lost(instance)` is one leaving, by a goodbye or by its records expiring. A change
-         to an instance's details (its port or TXT record) is not an event: resolve it again.
-         A `Browser` delivers these through `#events`.
-     entry .showable   renders an event as `found Elsinore._fury._tcp.local` or `lost …`
-   entry .Activity   what a backend reports as it works, logged through the `Loggable` at each loan
+         `Found(instance)` es una instancia que aparece (su registro PTR llega a la caché), y
+         `Lost(instance)` una que se va, por una despedida o porque sus registros caducan. Un
+         cambio en los detalles de una instancia (su puerto o su registro TXT) no es un evento:
+         hay que volver a resolverla. Un `Browser` entrega estos eventos a través de `#events`.
+     entry .showable   representa un evento como `found Elsinore._fury._tcp.local` o `lost …`
+   entry .Activity   lo que comunica un backend mientras trabaja, registrado a través del `Loggable` de cada préstamo

=   entry .Activity   what a backend reports as it works, logged through the `Loggable` at each loan
-     detail
+     detail

-         Each loan — an advertisement, a browse, a resolution — takes a `Discovery.Activity is
-         Loggable`, to which the backend reports what it does for that loan: `Probing(name)`
-         and `Yielded(name)` at `fine` level and `Conflicted(name)` while a name is being
-         claimed; `Claimed(instance)` and `Withdrawn(instance)` as an advertisement starts and
-         ends; `Browsing(service)` and `Resolved(instance)`. All are tagged `Log.Network`, and
-         the probing ones `Log.Protocol` as well. A backend holds no logger of its own, so its
-         background work between loans — defending a name, re-probing after a conflict — goes
-         unreported; `logging.silentLogging` satisfies the requirement when nothing is wanted.
+         Cada préstamo (un anuncio, una búsqueda, una resolución) recibe un `Discovery.Activity
+         is Loggable`, al que el backend comunica lo que hace para ese préstamo: `Probing(name)`
+         y `Yielded(name)` en el nivel `fine` y `Conflicted(name)` mientras se reclama un nombre;
+         `Claimed(instance)` y `Withdrawn(instance)` cuando un anuncio empieza y termina;
+         `Browsing(service)` y `Resolved(instance)`. Todos llevan la etiqueta `Log.Network`, y
+         los de sondeo también `Log.Protocol`. Un backend no tiene logger propio, así que su
+         trabajo en segundo plano entre préstamos (defender un nombre, volver a sondear tras un
+         conflicto) no se comunica; `logging.silentLogging` satisface el requisito cuando no se
+         quiere nada.

